Then there is the question of why do people play Nethack?  Of course,
I think my conception of the game is a valid one, and that wouldn't
drive too many people away from the game, and might attract other
players besides.  But there are many reasons people play, and don't
play, computer games.  There are lots of excellent games that are
rarely played, and for no fault of their own.  If you consider
popularity an objective measure of game quality, you'll find yourself
proclaiming a lot of bad games as being excellent.  As it stands, it's
looking more and more that even some -addictive- games might gain that
quality for reasons other than quality.  (I'm thinking of Peggle
here.)

