I disagree.  Negative exercise causes stats to degrade all the time,
mind flayers are usually encountered a few times in a successful game,
and strength losses are frequently encountered while trying to gain
poison resistance.

In fact.... note, the guiding principle around Nethack's construction
is to be something akin to a 1st Edition D&D simulator.  Many magic
items and monsters in the game take their cue from D&D's lead.  And
D&D had lots of sources of stat loss.  At the very least, venomous
monster attacks should drain stats more often, which happened all the
time in D&D and would also fit in with Rogue's Strength decay
mechanic.  (Which, after all, is where potions of restore ability came
from in the first place.)

