Stat drainers would be a good middle ground you know, if stat loss
couldn't just be instantly repaired.  Anyway, I've been starting to
work on a patch myself, don't know how far I get considering how
little-documented the source code is.  (That'd be a nice project for
the wiki, perhaps?  Listing out which functions are where and what
calls them, etc.)  Anyhow, one of the first things I've managed to
change is removing the restore ability function from unicorn horns,
and having them move a step towards cursed when applying one fixes a
trouble.  At least that way, to keep using a single horn for
restoration one has to keep blessing it, which eats into holy water
stocks, which also helps make the special conditions a little more
dangerous.

